---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const topics = [
  { n: "01", title: "Distributed systems", text: "Keeping services understandable, resilient and responsive as scale and complexity grow." },
  { n: "02", title: "Search & relevance", text: "The engineering behind discovery: relevance, latency, ranking and personalisation." },
  { n: "03", title: "Technical leadership", text: "Building shared context, making trade-offs explicit and helping teams do their best work." },
  { n: "04", title: "Systems thinking", text: "Connecting software to its operational setting, constraints and the people who use it." }
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Engineering — Chris Plössl" description="Engineering interests and approach to systems, software and technical leadership.">
  <section class="page-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow">Engineering</span>
    <h1>Good engineering is a team effort.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m drawn to the technical depth of building systems and the collaborative work of making those systems—and the teams behind them—better.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="work-grid" aria-label="Areas of interest">
    {topics.map((item) => <article class="work-card"><span class="eyebrow">{item.n} / Focus</span><h2>{item.title}</h2><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}
  </section>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>How I think about engineering</h2>
    <p>Architecture is a set of trade-offs. I value simple designs that make constraints visible, systems that can be operated confidently, and teams that understand why a decision was made.</p>
    <p>Technical leadership is useful when it gives people the context and room to make good decisions themselves. That takes clear communication, attention to outcomes and respect for the realities of the work.</p>
    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <p>My experience spans industrial automation and logistics, technical delivery, and software engineering. Working across these settings has kept my attention on the full system: how software meets operations, how decisions affect maintainability and how teams share responsibility.</p>
    <p>I keep this overview at the level of general experience. Specific project details, metrics and employer information belong here only when they are confirmed and appropriate to share publicly.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
